{"name":"Candelabra","hex":"#e1c161","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"candelabra","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of candelabrum"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A single candelabrum."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candelabra"}],"entries":[{"title":"Candelabra","blocks":[{"text":"A candelabrum, or candelabra, is a type of candlestick which has multiple branches to hold several candles as opposed to only one. \"Candelabra\" can be used to describe a variety of candle holders including chandeliers. However, candelabra can also be distinguished as freestanding branched candle holders that are placed on a surface such as the floor, a stand, or a tabletop. Chandeliers, on the other hand, are hung from the ceiling."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/WP_Z%C3%BCrich_Stammtisch_46_Leuchter.jpg/330px-WP_Z%C3%BCrich_Stammtisch_46_Leuchter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candelabra","wikidata":"Q548275"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/St._Matthews_Chancel.jpg/500px-St._Matthews_Chancel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/St._Matthews_Chancel.jpg/1280px-St._Matthews_Chancel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/St._Matthews_Chancel.jpg/500px-St._Matthews_Chancel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Candelabra located next to the high altar of St. Matthew's Evangelical Lutheran Church in Charleston, South Carolina","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASt._Matthews_Chancel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/1960_Royal_Court_of_Belgium.jpg/500px-1960_Royal_Court_of_Belgiu